sieve-filter-v2
; The ambitus: from the lowest note of a melody to its highest is at most `span` semitones, wherever
; it lies (melody-range-v1 bounds the register; this bounds how wide the tune is). Rests pass. The
; state is nothing yet (0), or the lowest note so far and how far above it the highest is:
; 1 + (low - 1) * (span + 1) + width.
id        melody-ambitus
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   notes*
describe  From the lowest note to the highest is at most the span, in semitones.
param     span  int  12  0  48  the widest the melody may be, lowest note to highest, in semitones

states    {1 + PITCHES * (span + 1)}
start     0
accept    0..{PITCHES * (span + 1)}
for d 0 {DURATIONS - 1}
  t 0 @{d} 0
  for q 1 {PITCHES}
    t 0 @{q * DURATIONS + d} {1 + (q - 1) * (span + 1)}
  done
  for lo 1 {PITCHES}
    for w 0 {span}
      if {lo + w <= PITCHES}
        t {1 + (lo - 1) * (span + 1) + w} @{d} {1 + (lo - 1) * (span + 1) + w}
        for q {max(1, lo + w - span)} {min(PITCHES, lo + span)}
          t {1 + (lo - 1) * (span + 1) + w} @{q * DURATIONS + d} {1 + (min(lo, q) - 1) * (span + 1) + max(lo + w, q) - min(lo, q)}
        done
      fi
    done
  done
done
end
